{"name":"No Way Rosé","hex":"#fbaa95","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"way","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Wayana."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["To do with a place or places.","A means to enter or leave a place."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/way"},{"term":"rosé","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative form of rosé wine."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ros%C3%A9"}],"entries":[{"title":"Rosé","blocks":[{"text":"A rosé is a type of wine that incorporates some of the color from the grape skins, but not enough to qualify it as a red wine. It may be the oldest known type of wine, as it is the most straightforward to make with the skin contact method. The pink color can range from a pale \"onionskin\" orange to a vivid near-purple, depending on the grape varieties used and winemaking techniques. Usually, the wine is labelled rosé in French, Portuguese, and English-speaking countries; rosado in Spanish; rosat in Catalan; or rosato in Italian."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f8/Ros%C3%A9_wine_-_July_2023_-_Sarah_Stierch_01-cropped.jpg/330px-Ros%C3%A9_wine_-_July_2023_-_Sarah_Stierch_01-cropped.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ros%C3%A9","wikidata":"Q12979"},{"title":"Rose (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Rose is the color halfway between red and magenta, whose hue corresponds to an angle of 330 degrees on the HSV/HSL color wheel."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2c/Pink-Rose-Sitia-Crete.jpg/330px-Pink-Rose-Sitia-Crete.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rose_(color)","wikidata":"Q533047"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f8/Ros%C3%A9_wine_-_July_2023_-_Sarah_Stierch_01-cropped.jpg/500px-Ros%C3%A